vsm2.13:26.1:
Just as when a strong man is felling a big tree for the purpose of making the peak of a gable, but is unable to fell the big
tree with an axe blade blunted by lopping the branches and foliage, still he does not give up the task; on the contrary,
he goes to a smithy and has his axe sharpened, after which he returns and continues chopping the tree;
